  "_comment": [
    "Real repositories, pinned by commit so a run is reproducible and a",
    "regression is attributable to brainkit rather than to upstream moving.",
    "Chosen to span the languages the shipped extractors claim, at two",
    "sizes, and to stay small enough that a full run is minutes rather than",
    "hours -- the question is coverage and cost per language, not throughput.",
    "Commits are the repositories' HEAD as of 2026-08-08, resolved with",
    "git ls-remote. Re-pin deliberately; do not track HEAD, or a coverage",
    "change will be indistinguishable from an upstream change.",
    "Fetched shallow into benchmarks/.cache (gitignored). A repository that",
    "cannot be fetched is skipped rather than fatal: this tier is opt-in and",
    "a network problem must not read as a brainkit regression."
  ],
